    "identifier": "stone-form",
    "description": "<p>If a creature in your weapons range would take a reaction, before their effect is applied, make a melee taijutsu attack. On a hit, you deal your [Weapons damage] + 3d8 and the affected creature must make a Strength Saving throw. On a failed save, the triggering jutsu is interrupted and its effects are dispelled, but the chakra is still spent.</p>\n<p>Chain 1: On a failed save the affected creature doubles the chakra spent.</p>\n<p>At Higher Ranks: For every rank you cast this jutsu above D-Rank, increase the cost by 3 and the damage by 1d8.</p>",
